# Handling Secrets Safely

This guide demonstrates best practices for managing secrets in applications.

## 1. Use a Secrets Manager
Store credentials in a dedicated service such as HashiCorp Vault or AWS Secrets Manager.

## 2. Inject at Runtime
```bash
export DB_PASSWORD=$(aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id db/password --query SecretString --output text)
```

## 3. Avoid Logging
Never include secret values in log files. Use placeholders like `[REDACTED]`.

## 4. Rotate Regularly
Implement automated rotation policies to limit exposure windows.

## 5. Validate Inputs
Always validate user input before using it in queries or commands.

## 6. Example: Node.js
```javascript
const { SecretManagerServiceClient } = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();
async function accessSecretVersion() {
  const name = 'projects/my-project/secrets/my-secret/versions/latest';
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({ name });
  const payload = version.payload.data;
  console.log('Secret data:', payload.toString());
}
```

Following these steps will keep your application secure.

