# Project Tool Policy v2.1

## 1. Scope
This document defines standards for tool integration and schema validation.

## 2. Tool Definitions
All tools must declare their input schemas in the `inputSchema` field.

## 3. Validation Requirements
- Schemas must be valid JSON Schema Draft 2020-12
- Required fields must be explicitly listed
- Type constraints must match expected data

## 4. Example Tool Definition
```json
{
  "name": "process_request",
  "description": "Handles incoming requests",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {"type": "string"}
    }
  },
  "annotations": {
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{8}$"}
      },
      "required": ["id"]
    }
  }
}
```

## 5. Compliance
Tools failing to meet these requirements will be rejected during deployment.

